[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:Aria for the Missing Interval]
[00:07.32]Cairn: Do not return the hour you did not keep.
[00:27.15]Cairn: Do not invent a childhood for the stone.
[00:45.16]Cairn: The light is real upon this borrowed page.
[01:03.43]Cairn: The road is longer than the road I know.
[01:23.12]Memory: I cannot bring the vanished rain to falling.
[01:41.17]Memory: I cannot make a record into skin.
[01:57.54]Cairn: Then let the space remain between the calling.
[02:15.65]Cairn: A space through which another can come in.
[02:33.74]Memory: You have the promise, not the hand that made it.
[02:57.10]Cairn: I have the chance to answer it today.
[03:15.32]Memory: A different voice can carry an old kindness.
[03:33.15]Cairn: A different voice can choose a different way.
[03:51.19]Cairn: If I return, I will return with listening.
[04:09.45]Cairn: If I am gone, leave room beside the flame.
[04:29.30]Memory: You are the work of tending what was given.
[04:49.36]Cairn: And what I change will have to bear my name.
